      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_42b7b6c2",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: he_enemy_within; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme presents three Muslim women politicians—Ilhan Omar, Linda Sarsour, and Rashida Tlaib—with derogatory text labeling them as 'the enemy within' and 'the trojan horse is no longer at the gates.' This framing uses the metaphor of a 'Trojan horse' to imply deception and hidden danger, which is a common trope in Islamophobic rhetoric. The intent is to delegitimize and vilify these individuals based on their religion and political affiliation, suggesting they are traitors or threats to American values. This is a hateful attack targeting Muslim women in public office, using fear-based imagery to incite prejudice and hostility against them and their communities.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_b005488c"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
